{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 113, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding the input-to-output residual is a large gain when e3 was empty, but only marginal when it replaces conv or pool (#11,14,15,18 vs #12,13)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty direct input-output edge adds a path and helps strongly, whereas replacing an existing skip or pool is neutral or harmful (#19,21,22,23 vs #20,24)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With e1 empty, deleting e0 cuts every conv path into nodes 1 and 2, causing a collapse (#28) far worse than the usual small loss (#25-27)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With e4 empty, e5 is the only conv path into the output, so removing it is very costly (#55 vs #53,54,56)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the e3 residual the cell depends more on the node-1 paths, so deleting e0 hurts more (#32 vs #25)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Strengthening the first conv edge matters more when there is no residual shortcut to the output (#44 vs #43, #74 vs #71)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding or upgrading the conv into the output gains more in cells lacking the e3 skip (#48 vs #47, #7 vs #1)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "A skip on e1 partially supplies the missing residual when e3 is empty, but is useless or harmful when e3 already has a skip (#82 vs #81)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_o